  "question_stem": "The diagram shows the vertical cross-section $XYZ$ of a rough slide. The section $YZ$ is a straight line of length $2\\text{ m}$ inclined at an angle of $\\alpha$ to the horizontal, where $\\sin \\alpha = 0.28$. The section $YZ$ is tangential to the curved section $XY$ at $Y$, and $X$ is $1.8\\text{ m}$ above the level of $Y$. A child of mass $25\\text{ kg}$ slides down the slide, starting from rest at $X$. The work done by the child against the resistance force in moving from $X$ to $Y$ is $50\\text{ J}$.",
